    "title": "Motorcyclist killed in three-vehicle crash in Tulsa identified - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago TULSA, Okla. — One person is deceased following a crash involving a motorcycle on the Broken Arrow Expressway.\nTulsa Police responded to a crash involving a motorcycle, a pickup truck, and an SUV on the Broken Arrow Expressway near 31st Street and Yale Avenue.\nAccording to officers, a motorcycle rider, identified as 25-year-old Daniel Hill, was moving at high speeds and hit the back of a pickup. The rider passed away as a result of the crash.\nDuring the accident, an SUV was also damaged, however both drivers of the pickup and the SUV were not injured.\nThis is an ongoing investigation, and FOX23 will continue to provide updates as more information becomes available.\n1",
    "summary": "1 days ago TULSA, Okla. — One person is deceased following a crash involving a motorcycle on the Broken Arrow Expressway. Tulsa Police responded to a crash involving a motorcycle, a pickup truck, and an SUV on the Broken Arrow Expressway near 31st Street and Yale Avenue. According to officers, a motorcycle rider, identified as 25-year-old Daniel Hill, was moving at high speeds and hit the back of a pickup. The rider passed away as a result of the crash. This is an ongoing investigation, and FOX23 will continue to provide updates as more information becomes available.",
